@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document rather than the whole new version. The library can apply RFC 6902 patches but cannot produce them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when passed to `applyPatch`.
+- The patch is minimal in the sense of locality: it descends into objects and arrays and emits operations only for what differs; unchanged members and items are never rewritten.
+- Array insertions and removals yield a single `add` / `remove` of that item; a moved item yields a remove and an add (or `move`), not rewrites of the items in between.
+- Inputs are never mutated and values in the patch do not alias the inputs.
+- Not breaking: purely additive; no existing export changes.
+
+Governing standard: RFC 6902 (JSON Patch) §4 (operations), §4.6 equality; RFC 6901 §3–§5 for pointer escaping of paths.
+
+Out of scope: `copy` and `test` operations, RFC 7396 merge-patch generation, patch optimization beyond the above (e.g. guaranteed globally shortest patch), and detecting moves between different parents.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch-diff`: generating an RFC 6902 JSON Patch from two JSON values.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new exported function and private helpers; `src/index.test.ts`: new tests.
+- No new dependencies; no `package.json` change.
